{
  "title": "Clavicle Shaft Fracture - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/322128/clavicle-shaft-fracture--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 4 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Clavicle Shaft Fractures are common pediatric fractures that most commonly occur due to a fall on an outstretched arm or direct trauma to lateral aspect of shoulder.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made with plain radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative management with a sling. Surgical management is indicated for open fractures or those associated with impending soft tissue compromise.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "2",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common; 15% pediatric upper extremity injuries",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "birth fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "0.5% normal deliveries;1.6% breech deliveries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "traumatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most often seen in active patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fall on an outstretched arm or direct trauma to lateral aspect of shoulder",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "birth fractures (account for 90% of obstetric fractures)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if there is no history of trauma consider congenital pseudarthrosis of clavicle (typically on right except in patients with dextrocardia)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "displacing forces",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**medial fragment displaces posterosuperior**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "due to pull of the sternocleidomastoid muscle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**lateral fragment displaces inferomedially**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "due to pull of pectoralis and weight of arm",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "open fractures buttonhole through platysma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "are rare but include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "neurovascular injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "brachial plexus injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "associated topics on orthobullets",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pediatric",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**medial clavicle physeal injury**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**clavicle shaft fracture - pediatric** (80%)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**distal clavicle physeal injury**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "adolescent and adult",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**sternoclavicular dislocation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**clavicle shaft fracture**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**distal third clavicle fracture**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Relevant Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Acromioclavicular Joint Anatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "AC joint stability",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/322128/images/d15b8680-a3c7-498d-8441-b831f8f5469e_ac_joint_natomy..jpg",
              "caption": "AC joint anatomy"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "static stabilizers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**acromioclavicular ligament**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "provides anterior/posterior stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "has superior, inferior, anterior, and posterior components",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**superior ligament** is strongest, followed by posterior",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**coracoclavicular ligaments** (trapezoid and conoid)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "provides superior/inferior stability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**conoid ligament is strongest**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**capsule**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "dynamic stabilizers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "deltoid and trapezius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
